  "problem": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}+y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{7}{12}.$",
